WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:10.200
Start from single nodes: each is its own cluster, and the cut is all 18 of the weight.

2
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.867
Each step merges the legal pair with the highest affinity.

3
00:00:14.867 --> 00:00:19.267
Affinity is the total weight between the two clusters.

4
00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:23.844
Stop when K is reached, or no legal pair remains.

5
00:00:24.244 --> 00:00:28.378
Step one: A–B and D–E both score 5.

6
00:00:28.378 --> 00:00:32.733
A tie goes by name: A before D, so A–B.

7
00:00:32.733 --> 00:00:35.978
The cut drops from 18 to 13.

8
00:00:36.378 --> 00:00:39.444
A and B contract into one cluster.

9
00:00:39.444 --> 00:00:50.022
AB and C share two wires, 1 + 4 = 5, tying D–E again; by members [A, B] < [D], so AB–C.

10
00:00:50.022 --> 00:00:53.044
The cut drops from 13 to 8.

11
00:00:53.444 --> 00:00:56.022
Step three: D–E.

12
00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:57.933
Merge them.

13
00:00:57.933 --> 00:01:02.733
Two clusters left, stop: ABC | DE, cut 3.

14
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:07.756
Every merge lowers the cut by exactly its affinity.

15
00:01:08.156 --> 00:01:12.756
The original page compared arrays with a plain less-than.

16
00:01:12.756 --> 00:01:20.667
JavaScript turns the arrays into strings first: “-1” sorts before “-5”.

17
00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:23.667
All four settings came out wrong.

18
00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:27.933
The fix: compare field by field, numbers as numbers.

19
00:01:28.333 --> 00:01:34.467
Capacity 2: AB plus C is 3, blocked, so D–E merges instead.

20
00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:38.467
After that, both candidates exceed the capacity.

21
00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:43.711
It stops at 3 clusters, cut 8: legal, but K is not reached.

22
00:01:44.111 --> 00:01:46.244
Four things to keep.

23
00:01:46.244 --> 00:01:50.711
Merge the legal pair with the most weight between them;

24
00:01:50.711 --> 00:01:54.178
ties by name, field by field;

25
00:01:54.178 --> 00:02:02.311
the cut drops by each affinity; with no legal pair, stop. Try it in the lab below.
